## 4. The gate's own matrix with the rows on the clone's `master` (exit 0)

    $ python3 tools/gate-registry-check.py --selftest
    PASS valid-row: exit=0 (want 0) line='registered 1 unregistered 0 defective 0' ...
    PASS thin-row: exit=1 (want 1) line='registered 1 unregistered 0 defective 3' ...
    PASS empty-exit-map: exit=1 (want 1) line='registered 1 unregistered 0 defective 1' ...
    PASS missing-path: exit=1 (want 1) line='defective .ufo/waves/round-98/count-selftest.py: missing-path:.ufo/waves/round-999/count-c999.py' ...
    PASS prose-only: exit=1 (want 1) line='registered 0 unregistered 1 defective 0' ...
    PASS lane-tip 92c387e21c94: exit=0 line='registered 44 unregistered 0 defective 0'
    GATE_SELFTEST pass=6 fail=0
    EXIT=0

Arm 6 (`gate-registry-check.py:369-383`) resolves `master` of the tool's own
checkout, not the working tree and not HEAD: on a clone still at the build
commit the lane arm reports the two counters unregistered until the rows are on
`master`. Here `master` was moved to the clone-local commit `92c387e2` for the
run; the lane's `master` was never touched.

## 5. Path-token hazard probe (clone only, reverted)

A scheme-prefixed URL in a row is safe (the regex lookbehind blocks the match
right after `//`), but a bare `host/org/.../file.ext` token is graded as a
repository path:

    $ printf '%s\n' "" "| Name | ... |" "|---|---|---|---|---|" \
        "| probe | measurement: \`python3 tools/round49-replay-witness-audit.py\` | 0 ok | \
         model huggingface.co/ggml-org/models-moved/resolve/499bc/tinyllamas/stories260K.gguf | read-only |" \
        >> SKILL.md
    $ python3 tools/gate-registry-check.py --repo $S/lane | tail -2
    defective tools/round49-replay-witness-audit.py: missing-path:huggingface.co/ggml-org/models-moved/resolve/499bc/tinyllamas/stories260K.gguf
    registered 44 unregistered 0 defective 1
    EXIT=1
    $ cp $S/skill-keep.md SKILL.md && python3 tools/gate-registry-check.py --repo $S/lane
    registered 44 unregistered 0 defective 0
    EXIT_reverted=0

The same row appended as a single `|` line with no header/separator above it is
ignored entirely (`registry_rows` requires a block of at least two lines), so a
stray row can neither register nor deregister a counter.

